      "narration": "When Rosa applies for disability coverage, the insurer collects personal information from her, her physicians, consumer reporting agencies and the MIB. Maryland’s insurance information and privacy protection law requires the insurer to tell her, in a notice of information practices, what kinds of information may be collected, from whom, how it may be used and disclosed, and her rights to see and correct it. Investigative consumer reports require their own notice and the right to be interviewed. Pretext interviews, in which someone pretends to be another person to pry information loose, are prohibited. The law applies to insurers and to producers acting for them.",
